WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.400
Edited app screenshots
Synthetic narration

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.155
BioGraph Steward connects a protein question to an inspectable evidence
graph.

00:00:06.155 --> 00:00:10.205
Open saved work, or create a scoped Pharos workspace locally.

00:00:10.205 --> 00:00:17.905
Ask a supported question, follow its graph and citations, inspect sources,
then save a review as a new run or export.

00:00:17.905 --> 00:00:20.805
We begin with the Added source context workspace.

00:00:20.805 --> 00:00:23.655
The shared site replays saved agent work.

00:00:23.655 --> 00:00:27.612
New live agent questions need a model; form-based readers do not.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.019
Pharos supplies the backbone.

00:00:31.019 --> 00:00:37.769
Native Gene Ontology location records and sequence-checked STRING
associations add traceable context.

00:00:37.769 --> 00:00:45.769
For KRAS and CDC42BPB, the source passport shows an association absent from
captured Pharos.

00:00:45.769 --> 00:00:51.293
Its provider, original record, identity checks and candidate status remain
visible.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:57.420
A published location reference covers 31 of the 99 targets.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:02.995
Both source views use this same subset, with 51 protein-location labels.

00:01:02.995 --> 00:01:08.914
The other 68 targets may still have app annotations; they have no matched
entry in this reference.

00:01:08.914 --> 00:01:15.690
Native Gene Ontology recovers 44 labels, versus 41 for captured Pharos.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:21.990
Some GO location annotations and the reference reuse Human Protein Atlas
observations.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:26.615
OpenCell supplies a separate, previously used research sensitivity check.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:33.016
Nemotron selects a supported source tool, such as the STRING association
reader.

00:01:33.016 --> 00:01:39.891
It matches the protein to the loaded cohort, checks the attached sources,
and validates the query arguments.

00:01:39.891 --> 00:01:44.866
The agent inspects selected citations and proposes review actions.

00:01:44.866 --> 00:01:50.397
This recorded investigation shows 8 of 14 matching proteins under its saved
limit.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:55.305
Open the manual reader for all 14 returned partners.

00:01:55.305 --> 00:01:58.155
Graph view focuses an individual result.

00:01:58.155 --> 00:02:00.680
Show all results restores the overview.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.005
Type a start entity and choose a connected destination.

00:02:04.005 --> 00:02:11.580
Try KRAS to CDC42BPB, TP53 to nucleus, or BRAF to a pathway.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.541
Results and evaluation explains the comparisons.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:22.484
For the demonstration, download the editable KRAS copy, extract it and run
its Python launcher.

00:02:22.484 --> 00:02:26.384
It includes the application, graph and preserved sources.

00:02:26.384 --> 00:02:31.464
Choose a claim, enter a reviewer, decision and reason, then save a new run.

00:02:31.464 --> 00:02:33.389
The original is preserved.

00:02:33.389 --> 00:02:35.483
The shared website stays read-only.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:40.430
A separate historical study tests protein function prediction.

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:45.430
LocalPlus is a published method that transfers known functions from
connected proteins.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:49.630
A learned model combines network, sequence and annotation context.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:52.655
Fmax summarizes the precision-recall balance.

00:02:52.655 --> 00:02:56.105
Higher is better; this is not percentage accuracy.

00:02:56.105 --> 00:03:05.405
In the primary evaluation of 1,954 proteins, it rises from 0.055 to 0.073.

00:03:05.405 --> 00:03:11.180
The sensitivity view rises from 0.172 to 0.210.

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:15.830
Paired intervals support both gains over retained LocalPlus within this
study.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:20.255
Extra gain beyond refreshed annotations remains uncertain.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:27.539
The second saved example, Qualified Pharos workspace, demonstrates applied
graph decisions.

00:03:27.539 --> 00:03:36.889
It excludes 298 records with obsolete Gene Ontology identifiers and retains
16,687.

00:03:36.889 --> 00:03:43.442
Every decision preserves its reason and original input, keeping the result
inspectable and recoverable.

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:49.463
These are demonstrations of one workflow, not separate applications.

00:03:49.463 --> 00:03:55.138
Source integration and applied decisions are illustrated by the two saved
workspaces.

00:03:55.138 --> 00:04:03.954
Location benchmarks and the historical prediction study assess the approach;
users do not need benchmark data to explore their own questions.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:10.833
Open the shared application without signing in, then follow a question to
its sources.

00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:17.933
The final handoff includes the report, demonstration, slides, and one
indexed app and graph package.

00:04:17.933 --> 00:04:20.741
Download the editable example to continue locally.
